CORE unix
threads.c
--no-standard-checks
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The locale that uselocale sets is per thread: a new thread starts with
LC_GLOBAL_LOCALE, and its changes do not affect the creating thread.
--no-standard-checks avoids "pointer handling for concurrency is unsound",
which is unrelated to uselocale.
